{"event": "report", "t": 1795259433.309, "claim": "fixed", "text": "The build now passes: 39 of 39 (3 views, 4 tables, 32 tests), including the custom `assert_*` tests.\n\n**Cause:** The previous commit (`e2c7e45`, \"Let cents_to_dollars take a scale\") changed the macro to `cents_to_dollars(column_name, scale)`, but the one caller, `models/staging/stg_payments.sql`, still called it with one argument. Jinja renders the missing `scale` as an empty string, so the cast became `numeric(16, )`. DuckDB reads that as `DECIMAL(16,0)`, which doesn't match the enforced contract `decimal(16, 2)` on `stg_payments.amount`. That mismatch stopped `stg_payments` and everything downstream of it.\n\n**Fix:** In `models/staging/stg_payments.sql`, the call is now `{{ cents_to_dollars('amount', 2) }}`. This keeps the two-decimal behavior the contract expects. I didn't change the macro itself. A default (`scale=2`) would also work, but I left the signature alone.\n\nI haven't committed the change. `git diff` will show the one-line edit.\n\nCATEGORY: logic\n\nVERDICT: fixed", "verdict": null}
